        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="CLA02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <forename>Charles</forename>
                        <surname>Clairmont</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1795">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1850"/>
                    <occupation>bookseller</occupation>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Son of <persName key="CLA01">Mary Jane Godwin</persName> and Godwin's step-son.
    Godwin helped with his education and arranged for him to be apprenticed to <persName key="CON01">Constable</persName> in Edinburgh in 1811
    so as to learn the book trade, in the hope that he might run Godwin's business.  He returns to London in 1814.  He left England in 1816.</p>
                        <p> In 1828 Charles returned to England with his family and Godwin recorded visits of the family as 'Cts'. 
  These are accordingly  coded as Charles Clairmont.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>, 'Mary Jane Godwin'</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">St Clair, p. 395 and p. 477.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
